<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>skepsis report — {{ verdict.level }}</title>
<script>{{ plotly_js | safe }}</script>
<style>
  :root { --strong:#1a7f37; --moderate:#9a6700; --weak:#bc4c00; --likely_overfit:#cf222e; }
  body { font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif; margin: 0; color: #1f2937;
         background: #f8fafc; }
  main { max-width: 960px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 24px 16px 64px; }
  .banner { padding: 20px 24px; border-radius: 12px; color: white; margin-bottom: 24px; }
  .banner h1 { margin: 0 0 4px; font-size: 28px; }
  .banner p { margin: 0; opacity: .9; }
  section { background: white; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 12px;
            padding: 20px 24px; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  h2 { font-size: 18px; margin: 0 0 12px; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; }
  td, th { text-align: left; padding: 6px 12px 6px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid #f1f5f9;
           font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .reason { padding: 4px 0; }
  .warn { color: #9a6700; }
  .skip { color: #64748b; font-style: italic; }
  footer { color: #64748b; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.6; }
  .overflow { overflow-x: auto; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <div class="banner" style="background: var(--{{ verdict.level | lower }});">
    <h1>{{ verdict.level.replace("_", " ") }}</h1>
    <p>skepsis {{ meta.skepsis_version }} &middot; {{ meta.n_obs }} observations
       &middot; {{ n_trials_text }} &middot; freq: {{ meta.freq }}</p>
  </div>

  <section>
    <h2>Verdict rationale</h2>
    {% for reason in verdict.reasons %}<div class="reason">&#8226; {{ reason }}</div>{% endfor %}
    <p><em>The verdict is a documented, overridable heuristic — read the diagnostics
    below, not just the label.</em></p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Summary</h2>
    <div class="overflow"><table>
      <tr><th>Metric</th><th>Value</th></tr>
      <tr><td>Annualized Sharpe (observed)</td><td>{{ "%.3f" | format(psr.sharpe_annualized) }}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Probabilistic Sharpe Ratio (vs 0)</td><td>{{ "%.4f" | format(psr.value) }}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Deflated Sharpe Ratio ({{ n_trials_text }})</td><td>{{ "%.4f" | format(dsr.value) }}</td></tr>
      {% if pbo %}<tr><td>Probability of Backtest Overfitting</td><td>{{ "%.3f" | format(pbo.value) }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
      {% if bootstrap %}<tr><td>Bootstrap no-skill p-value</td><td>{{ "%.4f" | format(bootstrap.p_value_no_skill) }}</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Max drawdown (95% CI)</td><td>{{ "%.1f" | format(bootstrap.drawdown_obs * 100) }}%
        ({{ "%.1f" | format(bootstrap.drawdown_ci[0] * 100) }}&ndash;{{ "%.1f" | format(bootstrap.drawdown_ci[1] * 100) }}%)</td></tr>{% endif %}
      {% if sensitivity %}<tr><td>Parameter stability score</td><td>{{ stability_text }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
    </table></div>
  </section>

  <section><h2>Equity curve</h2>{{ figures.equity | safe }}</section>

  <section>
    <h2>Deflated Sharpe</h2>
    <p>Observed periodic Sharpe {{ "%.4f" | format(psr.sharpe_periodic) }} against an
    expected max of {{ "%.4f" | format(dsr.benchmark_sr) }} from
    {{ n_trials_text }} (skew {{ "%.2f" | format(psr.skewness) }},
    kurtosis {{ "%.2f" | format(psr.kurtosis) }}).</p>
  </section>

  {% if pbo %}<section><h2>Probability of Backtest Overfitting</h2>{{ figures.pbo | safe }}</section>{% endif %}
  {% if bootstrap %}<section><h2>Bootstrap</h2>
    <p>Stationary bootstrap, mean block length {{ "%.1f" | format(bootstrap.mean_block_length) }},
    {{ bootstrap.n_resamples }} resamples.</p>{{ figures.bootstrap | safe }}</section>{% endif %}
  {% if sensitivity %}<section><h2>Parameter sensitivity</h2>{{ figures.sensitivity | safe }}</section>{% endif %}

  {% if skipped %}
  <section>
    <h2>Diagnostics that could not run</h2>
    {% for name, why in skipped.items() %}<div class="skip">{{ name }}: {{ why }}</div>{% endfor %}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% if warnings %}
  <section>
    <h2>Warnings</h2>
    {% for w in warnings %}<div class="warn">&#9888; {{ w }}</div>{% endfor %}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <footer>
    <p><strong>Methodology.</strong>
    PSR/DSR: Bailey &amp; L&oacute;pez de Prado (2012, 2014).
    Probability of Backtest Overfitting via CSCV: Bailey, Borwein, L&oacute;pez de Prado
    &amp; Zhu (2015). Stationary bootstrap: Politis &amp; Romano (1994); block length:
    Politis &amp; White (2004). Generated by
    <a href="https://github.com/abhinay/skepsis">skepsis</a> {{ meta.skepsis_version }}
    &middot; <a href="https://abhinay.github.io/skepsis">docs</a>.</p>
  </footer>
</main>
</body>
</html>
